{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "17862070",
      "title": "Important CLI Commands",
      "lectureOrder": 738,
      "videoOrder": 678,
      "sourceHash": "985dd21be5fc1aeb3083a0a0fab073a4d57bfff8c9b16487d8b372e39955b27b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.65,
          "en": "Instructor: So before we explore this angular.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.65,
          "end": 8.31,
          "en": "let's see which Angular CLI commands we can use inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.31,
          "end": 9.18,
          "en": "of a project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.18,
          "end": 11.46,
          "en": "We used ng new outside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.46,
          "end": 14.22,
          "en": "Now we can basically use all remaining commands inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.22,
          "end": 15.053,
          "en": "of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.053,
          "end": 18.51,
          "en": "Now you can type ng help here, not ng --help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 21.66,
          "en": "but just ng help to learn about all the commands.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.66,
          "end": 22.98,
          "en": "And of course as mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "you have that page in the official documentation there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 29.823,
          "en": "Under CLI commands, you also see all the commands.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "Now some commands are really niche commands",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.95,
          "end": 36.78,
          "en": "which you'll rarely need, but of course there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.78,
          "end": 39.12,
          "en": "are also some commands which you'll need all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.12,
          "end": 40.53,
          "en": "For example, ng serve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.53,
          "end": 43.59,
          "en": "You know this one, it serves your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "Now just as before, if you add --help there after",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 48.27,
          "en": "you get details about this command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.27,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "and you can see there are quite some flags you can set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.69,
          "end": 54.03,
          "en": "Now, not all these flags are required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 54.03,
          "end": 57.45,
          "en": "of course, the defaults work just fine, but for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.45,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "you can set a port flag here to use a different port",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "than the default of 4,200.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 68.07,
          "en": "You can add --prod to actually serve your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.07,
          "end": 70.92,
          "en": "in production mode to have kind of an idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.92,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "of how it will work once you do build it for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 76.89,
          "en": "This however, is not something you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.89,
          "end": 77.723,
          "en": "on a real web server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.723,
          "end": 78.99,
          "en": "It's not production ready",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 78.99,
          "end": 82.28999999999999,
          "en": "it's just a preview of how production mode will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.28999999999999,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "You also have --open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "This will actually tell the CLI to not only serve the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "but to open the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 92.85,
          "en": "in a new browser tab once it's done serving it up so that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.85,
          "end": 96.47999999999999,
          "en": "so that you don't have to manually open it there and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.47999999999999,
          "end": 98.43,
          "en": "There are a bunch of configuration options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.43,
          "end": 99.45,
          "en": "you can set there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.45,
          "end": 102.66,
          "en": "Again, most of them are rarely needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 102.66,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "but if you do need them, well here they are as mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 108.9,
          "en": "Over time they might change, but still this command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 108.9,
          "end": 111.42,
          "en": "and the official docs here are a great place to learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 111.42,
          "end": 112.253,
          "en": "about them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 116.72999999999999,
          "en": "Now, besides ng serve, we also got ng generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 121.73,
          "en": "and ng generate with --help allows us to generate things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.58,
          "end": 124.23,
          "en": "in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 124.23,
          "end": 127.14,
          "en": "Here are the things we can generate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.14,
          "end": 128.97,
          "en": "You saw a couple of them throughout the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 128.97,
          "end": 131.85,
          "en": "like components, directives, but you could also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.85,
          "end": 134.88,
          "en": "generate guards or services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 134.88,
          "end": 139.35,
          "en": "You could generate pipes or modules, interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 139.35,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "and interceptors for the HTTP client and application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 145.02,
          "en": "which is something I'll come back to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.02,
          "end": 148.8,
          "en": "And some niche things like a serviceworker or a webworker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "You'll also see additional flags here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 153.27,
          "en": "But to see all the available flags, you should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.27,
          "end": 154.44,
          "en": "a bit more specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.44,
          "end": 158.13,
          "en": "And for example, say ng generate component --help to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.13,
          "end": 161.55,
          "en": "see how you can configure the generation of a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.55,
          "end": 164.16,
          "en": "And there you see that there are again a bunch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 164.16,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "of configuration options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 168.63,
          "en": "Now this might by the way be overwhelming by now, but keep",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.63,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "in mind that you don't have to learn those by heart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 174.75,
          "en": "The default will work just fine in most situations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 174.75,
          "end": 178.32,
          "en": "Just when you find that a default doesn't work for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 178.32,
          "end": 181.14,
          "en": "You might want to look into these configuration flags here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 181.14,
          "end": 183.51,
          "en": "and see whether you can change the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 183.51,
          "end": 185.04,
          "en": "to give you the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 185.04,
          "end": 186.78,
          "en": "or whatever you're trying to generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "in the way you want it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 190.35,
          "en": "For example, to not use inline styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 190.35,
          "end": 194.7,
          "en": "to not use inline templates to change the default prefix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.7,
          "end": 199.23,
          "en": "which is added to not generate test files and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 199.23,
          "end": 201.21,
          "en": "And of course this does not just exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 201.21,
          "end": 204.54,
          "en": "for the component generation but for pipes and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.54,
          "end": 207.48,
          "en": "So ng generate of course, is an important command.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 207.48,
          "end": 211.32,
          "en": "ng lint uses this tslint file I mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 211.32,
          "end": 212.73,
          "en": "It will now basically go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 212.73,
          "end": 215.31,
          "en": "through your entire setup and tell you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 215.31,
          "end": 218.67000000000002,
          "en": "if you have any linting errors and here everything passed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 218.67000000000002,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "But for example, if I go to the app component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 225.72,
          "en": "and I do remove this prefix app route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.72,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "and I watch lint again, it should tell me about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 231.243,
          "en": "So let's wait for this to finish.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 233.82,
          "end": 235.71,
          "en": "And indeed it found lint error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 235.71,
          "end": 237.27,
          "en": "And now it tells you that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 237.27,
          "end": 241.44,
          "en": "in the app component file in line four here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 241.44,
          "end": 244.83,
          "en": "the selector should be kebab-cased and include a dash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 244.83,
          "end": 245.76,
          "en": "So it tells me",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 245.76,
          "end": 248.4,
          "en": "that I'm not following this recommended practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 248.4,
          "end": 250.5,
          "en": "of naming my components like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 250.5,
          "end": 251.34,
          "en": "So that's linting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 251.34,
          "end": 252.78,
          "en": "And you can always use this lint command",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 252.78,
          "end": 255.6,
          "en": "from time to time to check your code quality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 255.6,
          "end": 256.77,
          "en": "ng build, of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 256.77,
          "end": 259.65,
          "en": "is all that important command to build your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 259.65,
          "end": 260.91,
          "en": "with --prod.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 260.91,
          "end": 262.32,
          "en": "You build it for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 262.32,
          "end": 264.63,
          "en": "So you optimize it as much as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 264.63,
          "end": 267.15,
          "en": "And you also saw before in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 267.15,
          "end": 269.73,
          "en": "in the deployment section that this will generate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 269.73,
          "end": 273.33,
          "en": "a dist folder where you find your generated project files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 273.33,
          "end": 274.38,
          "en": "which you then can put",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 274.38,
          "end": 277.62,
          "en": "onto a server to well serve your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 277.62,
          "end": 280.83,
          "en": "from there and to really serve your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 280.83,
          "end": 283.95,
          "en": "to all the users out there in the world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 283.95,
          "end": 285.933,
          "en": "So here is this dist folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 286.77,
          "end": 289.08,
          "en": "Now I will come back to deployment a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 289.08,
          "end": 291.12,
          "en": "You learned how you can deploy it, but actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 291.12,
          "end": 292.98,
          "en": "there also is a different way of deploying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 292.98,
          "end": 294.177,
          "en": "with help of the CLI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 294.177,
          "end": 296.37,
          "en": "And as mentioned, I will come back to that for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 296.37,
          "end": 297.63,
          "en": "Let's ignore it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 297.63,
          "end": 300.21,
          "en": "So these are the CLI commands, and again, I pointed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 300.21,
          "end": 302.79,
          "en": "at it before, but check out the official docs to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 302.79,
          "end": 306.39,
          "en": "about all the commands and all the configuration options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 306.39,
          "end": 308.61,
          "en": "There are some commands like ng update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 308.61,
          "end": 310.77,
          "en": "and ng add and ng deploy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 313.773,
          "en": "and which we'll have a closer look in this module though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 315,
          "end": 316.2,
          "en": "Before we do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 316.2,
          "end": 318.6,
          "en": "let's analyze the angular.json file though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 318.6,
          "end": 321.12,
          "en": "because that configures our project in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 321.12,
          "end": 323.613,
          "en": "And thus far we didn't have a closer look yet.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
